+## LoadedInstructions and status rule
+
+- `delivered()` assumes two things: omitted parts are a prefix of the render order, and the cut part is the last part. `fit_hook` (bootstrap/instructions.rs:451-518) guarantees both. It drops parts from the front, and it only cuts when even the last part alone overflows. In that case `omitted` is every earlier label.
+- `cut_body_bytes` ends on a `\n` boundary, so `body.get(..n)` never falls back to the whole body.
+- The status comparison matches by label. It treats a digest or delivery-mode change as modified, and handles added and removed parts as the spec says. Omitted parts are never compared.
+- Read failures, corrupt JSON and other schemas all map to `unknown`. Write failures are swallowed.
+- `clone_view` walks history only when a clone is stale. A walk error only drops the commit column.
+
+## Stack view
+
+- Every field in the stack JSON is present: `harness_files_note`, `imports_followed: false`, `hook {cap, kept, omitted, cut}`, and a per-clone `instructions` object that is the same as the roster's.
+- A failed render becomes the seat's `error` row, and its clones read `error`.
+- `manifest()` propagates a `last_touches` failure as a whole-command error. The roster swallows the same failure. The two are inconsistent but harmless, because the walker is lenient on malformed records.
+
+## Harness files
+
+- Discovery follows the spec table. Codex is bounded by the Git root, the override shadows `AGENTS.md`, and the user files are `CODEX_HOME` and `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`. Claude walks every ancestor, with `.claude/rules/**/*.md` and the `AGENTS.md` fallback gated on no `CLAUDE.md`/`CLAUDE.local.md` at or above the cwd.
+- The merge keeps the first insertion's origin and env. The Claude ancestor walk runs before the user-level add, and that ordering causes the defect below.
+
+## Verdict
+not ready (user-level ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md mislabelled as ancestor without env: inspector; Codex "session id form differs" note cannot fire for Herdr's rollout-path form)
+
+## Must fix before landing
+- src/inspect/harness_files.rs:217-248 (spec 2.3, harness_files `origin` and `env: inspector`): when the cwd is under $HOME and CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR is unset (the default setup), the ancestor walk inserts $HOME/.claude/CLAUDE.md first with origin `ancestor` and env None. The user-level add then hits the existing entry, so the user file is reported as `origin: ancestor` without `env: inspector`. A review probe test (cwd home/proj, user.claude = home/.claude) printed `origin=Ancestor env=None`. Fix: run the user-level adds before the ancestor walk, or let a user-level add override origin and env on an existing entry.
+- src/inspect/loaded.rs:229-236 (spec 2.3, Codex `note: "codex session id form differs"`): the occupant's Codex id is already a file stem (observe/sessions.rs:38-45 stems a Herdr `AgentSession::Path`; the herdr wire test uses a rollout `.jsonl` path). A Codex rollout stem is `rollout-<timestamp>-<uuid>`, while the SessionStart payload `session_id` is the bare uuid. `stem(loaded) == stem(occupant)` therefore never holds for this form difference: the clone reads `unknown` with no note, which is the silent degraded state that spec 2.1 forbids. The spec also asks hg-blw.12 to record which form a real or documented payload uses, and nothing in this cluster records it. Fix: detect the form difference (for example, the occupant stem ends with `-<payload id>`) for the note only, without treating the ids as a match, and add a test with a rollout-path occupant.
+
+## Untested scope
+- No test uses a Codex occupant whose native id came from a Herdr rollout path together with a uuid payload id. `codex_form_differs_note` only covers a full path against the bare stem, which production never produces.
+- No test runs harness-file discovery with a cwd under the user's home, which is the default layout and the one that triggers the origin and env collision.
+- `instructions stack` has no test where `HistoryWalker::last_touches` fails, which ends the whole command rather than dropping the `path last touched` column.
+- Roster and stack instruction status for retired seats and clones under `--all` (render against an archived seat) is not exercised.
+- Roster and log behavior when a historical commit's tree holds an unparseable record still has no test (carried over from the earlier review).
+- Roster `last_change` cost near the 5000-commit cap with many seats has no measurement (carried over).
+
+## Deferred OK
+- Roster text (roster.rs `instructions_text`) shows the status and a truncated flag but not the spec 2.2 "count of parts loaded"; the JSON `parts` array carries it.
+- Stack text lists the loaded record's omitted labels but not its delivered part labels for a stale or unknown clone; the JSON `instructions.parts` carries them.
+- stack.rs `manifest()` fails the whole command on a `last_touches` error, while roster `clone_view` swallows the same failure; this is inconsistent but rare.
+- `loaded::clone_view` builds a fresh HistoryWalker per stale clone; that cost is acceptable at current instance sizes.
+- The earlier deferred minors for this cluster (dangling-parent check scope, swallowed manager error, noisy error rows for retired seats, brittle source-scan test, log `paths_at` cost) still apply unchanged.
